REGENT OF SUKAMARA

CENTRAL KALIMANTAN PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SUKAMARA REGENCY NUMBER 9 OF 2022

CONCERNING

WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

THE REGENT OF SUKAMARA,

Considering : a. that every woman and child has equal rights to live a dignified life in accordance with the principles of humanity, equality and justice;

b. that to ensure women's empowerment and child protection in accordance with talents and human dignity and to receive protection from violence, discrimination and other violations, women's empowerment and child protection must be carried out in an integrated, continuous manner through the acceleration of the fulfillment and protection of the rights of women and children in their personal lives, family, community, nation and state;

c. that pursuant to the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b, Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning

Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, women's empowerment and child protection is one of the mandatory government affairs that is the authority of regional governments;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b, and c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and

Child Protection;

In View of : 1. Article 18 Paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 5 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Katingan Regency, Seruyan Regency, Sukamara Regency, Lamandau Regency, Gunung Mas Regency, Pulang Pisau Regency, Murung Raya Regency and

Barito Timur Regency in Central Kalimantan Province

(State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 18, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number

3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);

4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

5. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Crime of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

6. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

7. Government Regulation Number 43 of 2017 concerning the Implementation of Restitution for Children Who Are Victims of Criminal Acts (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2017 Number 219, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6131);

8. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Policy Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;

9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 446);

10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2011 concerning the National Socio-Cultural Strategy to Realize Gender Equality (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 20);

11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 of 2011 concerning Policy for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 12 of 2011 concerning Indicators for Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;

13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 13 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities;

14. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning the System for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 615);

15. Regional Regulation of Sukamara Regency Number 6 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus of Sukamara Regency (Regional Gazette of Sukamara

Regency of 2016 Number 6, Supplement to the Regional

Gazette of Sukamara Regency Number 40), as amended by Regional Regulation of Sukamara Regency

